  "answer_text": "The thin shirts from Columbia\u2019s **PFG (Performance Fishing Gear)** line are called different names depending on whether you are looking for a button-down or an athletic long-sleeve/hoodie. \n\nThe most popular options include:\n\n### 1. **The Tamiami (or Tamiami II)** \u2014 *The Ultra-Thin Button-Down*\nIf you are thinking of the super-thin, paper-light button-down shirt with chest pockets and a vented back, it is called the **Tamiami**.\n* **Why it\u2019s so thin:** It is made of **100% polyester ripstop fabric**, which is incredibly lightweight, silky to the touch, and feels airy. \n* **Key features:** Mesh-lined back vents, snap-button or velcro chest pockets, and built-in UPF sun protection. \n* *Note:* It is often confused with the **Bahama**, but the Bahama is made of nylon, making it noticeably thicker, stiffer, and heavier.\n\n### 2. **The Terminal Tackle** \u2014 *The Thin Sun Shirt / Hoodie*\nIf you are thinking of the thin, silky, athletic long-sleeve shirt (often with a hood or a crew neck) that has \"Columbia\" written down the sleeve, it is called the **Terminal Tackle**.\n* **Why it's so thin:** It is a performance knit shirt made of quick-drying, lightweight polyester with Omni-Wick and Omni-Shade sun protection. It is designed to feel like a second skin and keep you cool in direct sunlight.\n\n### 3. **The Slack Tide** \u2014 *The Thin Casual Camp Shirt*\nIf you are looking for a thin button-down but want a cleaner, more casual look without the heavy utility pockets and rod-holder loops on the chest, it is called the **Slack Tide**. \n* It is made of a very soft, lightweight, and slightly stretchy polyester fabric that breathes exceptionally well in the heat.\n\n### Summary of how they compare:\n* **Tamiami:** Paper-thin, silky polyester button-down with pockets.\n* **Terminal Tackle:** Thin, stretchy long-sleeve athletic/sun shirt (non-button-down).\n* **Slack Tide:** Thin, casual short-sleeve button-down (no heavy chest pockets).\n* **Bahama:** Medium-weight, crisp nylon button-down (feels thicker/stiffer than the Tamiami).\n* **Bonehead:** Heavy-weight, 100% cotton canvas button-down (the thickest option).",
